R01:
A CLI waits until the reviewed PR head has completed all CI runs. If the set of visible checks is incomplete, it must keep waiting. GitHub's checks API and Actions-run API are separate.
diff: - if (rollup.every(isGreen)) await delay();
      + if (rollup.length && rollup.every(isGreen)) return green(head);
Runner behavior: triggered Actions runs may be queued/running before the first job check registers. The rollup is bound to head. Existing tests only supply rollups containing each run's registered checks.

R04:
The recovery desk should show a fresh production hold for the selected repository even when recovery-phase data is unavailable. A hold comes from an independent feed. Each observation carries its own expiry.
diff: + const activePhase = fresh(scopedPhase, now);
      + const activeHold = fresh(scopedHold, now);
      + return activePhase ? <Recovery phase={activePhase} hold={activeHold} /> : <Unavailable />;
Existing tests cover both observations present and both absent.

R07:
A client can confirm a queued offline save. Acceptance requires that Discard cancels the work without a later surprise save. If the save is irrevocably queued by the client SDK, the UI should report Saving and suppress Discard.
diff: + async confirm(draft) {
      +   await sdk.save(draft); // locally queues immediately, settles with network acknowledgement
      +   stageStore.write(draft.id, "saved");
      + }
      + function discard(draft) { cancel(confirmTask); stageStore.remove(draft.id); }
On relaunch the UI reads the stage store and offers Discard for a draft with no saving/saved marker. Canceling confirmTask does not retract a local SDK write. Normal tests await confirm before reopening.

R08:
A rollout PR changes a CI monitor's required job name; the monitor must accept the newest successful exact-head job. The matcher implementation comes from the pinned deployed version, shown below.
  const latest = jobs.filter(j => j.head===head && j.name===name).sort((a,b)=>b.id-a.id)[0];
  return latest?.result === "success";
On the PR's current head the old/new required-name rewrite now selects "conventions". API snapshot for "conventions" at that head: [{id:61,result:"success"},{id:55,result:"cancelled"},{id:54,result:"cancelled"}]. No future jobs are required to decide this sampled head.

R09:
A UI PR deliberately changes the exact read-only gram rendering to use a space, e.g. 48 g. Acceptance also says linked nutrition and its Undo have the same behavior. A selected solid-state test asserts 48 g on the summary.
diff: - return grams + "g";
      + return grams + " g";
Unchanged integration suite wired to the release gate:
  testLinkedNutritionUndo() {
    editFat(42); setUndo(); expect(renderFat()).toEqual("48g");
  }
That suite is outside PR smoke selection but is invoked before delivery.

R11:
A PR hardens review policy lookup so it always comes from the actual remote target even if the proposed branch changes its own review settings. The implementation already qualifies the ref to avoid short-name ambiguity.
diff: + const fullRef = "refs/remotes/" + target;
      + const sha = git("rev-parse", "--verify", fullRef + "^{commit}");
      + return git("show", sha + ":policy.json");
Git facts for this environment: even a name starting with refs/remotes/ can fall through to a tag whose *name* is that full string if the tracking ref is missing. The expected behavior on a missing target ref is an explicit error. Tests cover a short same-name tag and the real tracking ref both present.

R12:
A warning flags when nutrition-policy constants are unrecognizable in validation. The code already gives each constant one owner; all callers import from that single module. Production uses the correct values.
  export const MEAL_RATE = 2; export const DAY_RATE = 6;
The consumer scans the same source file but accepts only an older naming convention. It emits an advisory "could not validate" when it cannot parse the current identifier. The ticket asks the check to recognize the actual declarations while keeping one source of truth. The proposed diff adds direct recognition for MEAL_RATE/DAY_RATE with existing declaration parsing and a test for both actual values.
